<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Surkhay Khan I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 1748</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Surkhay Khan I was khan of Kazikumukh, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lak">Lak</a> state in the mountains of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dagestan">Dagestan</a>, in the first half of the 18th century. Allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hajji-davud">Hajji Davud</a>, he sacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shamakhi">Shamakhi</a> in 1721 and afterwards ruled Shirvan for a time under Ottoman protection. He later resisted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nader-shah">Nader Shah</a>'s campaigns in Dagestan.</p></div>
